  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-tool-user-memory",
      "text": "[![npm][npm-badge]][npm] [![CI][ci-badge]][ci] [![MIT][license-badge]][license]\n\n这是一个给 DeepSeek Harness 使用的用户记忆插件。它保存你的个人背景和回答偏好，让新对话也能继续参考这些信息。\n\n[English][english] · [下载 0.4.2][release] · [更新日志][changelog]"
    },
    {
      "section": "能做什么",
      "text": "你可以像平时一样聊天，比如告诉助手“我主要做 Java 后端开发”或“我习惯用中文”。遇到明确的个人信息时，助手可以自动记录，并在回答下方显示“已记住”和“撤销”。\n\n记忆管理页可以搜索、新增、编辑和删除内容。页面右上角有启用开关，不想使用时关掉即可。\n\n需要手动核对的建议可以在“待确认”里保存或忽略。换电脑时，可以用“备份与迁移”导出数据，再到另一台电脑导入。\n\n![记忆管理界面][memory-image]"
    },
    {
      "section": "安装",
      "text": "先安装 DeepSeek Harness，再到 [0.4.2 发布页][release] 下载 `dsh-tool-user-memory-0.4.2.tgz`。在下载目录运行下面的命令，安装后重启 DSH。\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-tool-user-memory-0.4.2.tgz\n```\n\n示例使用 `web` 配置。如果你使用其他配置，把命令中的 `web` 换成对应名称。"
    },
    {
      "section": "使用",
      "text": "在 DSH 中打开“插件”，找到这个插件并点击“管理记忆”。已有内容会显示在列表里，也可以点击“新增记忆”手动添加。\n\n平时不用特意说“请记住”，明确的个人背景、技能熟悉度、语言和表达偏好都可以自动记录。记错了就点击回答下方的“撤销”，也可以到管理页修改或删除。\n\n启用后，后续对话会自动带上已保存的用户记忆。助手提出的待确认内容需要你保存后才会生效，替换已有内容时会显示新旧对照。"
    },
    {
      "section": "记什么，不记什么",
      "text": "这个插件只记录跟你本人有关的信息。项目配置、代码约束、发布规定和临时要求不会作为自动记忆保存，判断不明确时会跳过。\n\n记忆保存在本机，使用时会发送给你配置的模型服务。关闭或删除记忆会影响后续读取，已经发出的对话内容和已有备份仍会保留。"
    },
    {
      "section": "从源码运行",
      "text": "克隆仓库后，安装依赖并构建。下面使用本地路径安装，替换成你自己的仓库绝对路径即可。\n\n```sh\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm run build\ndsh plugin --profile web add \"link:/absolute/path/dsh-tool-user-memory\"\n```\n\nWindows 路径可以写成 `D:/projects/dsh-tool-user-memory`。重新构建后也需要重启 DSH。"
    },
    {
      "section": "从源码运行",
      "text": "[npm-badge]: https://img.shields.io/npm/v/dsh-tool-user-memory\n[npm]: https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-tool-user-memory\n[ci-badge]: https://github.com/IAMLieutenant/dsh-tool-user-memory/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg\n[ci]: https://github.com/IAMLieutenant/dsh-tool-user-memory/actions/workflows/ci.yml\n[license-badge]: https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue\n[license]: LICENSE\n[english]: README.en.md\n[release]: https://github.com/IAMLieutenant/dsh-tool-user-memory/releases/tag/v0.4.2\n[changelog]: CHANGELOG.md\n[memory-image]: docs/images/user-memory-list.png"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-tool-user-memory",
      "text": "[![npm][npm-badge]][npm] [![CI][ci-badge]][ci] [![MIT][license-badge]][license]\n\nA user memory plugin for DeepSeek Harness. It saves personal background and preferences so new conversations can use them too.\n\n[中文说明][chinese] · [Download 0.4.2][release] · [Changelog][changelog]"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "Tell the assistant about yourself as you normally would, such as your professional background or preferred language. Clear personal information can be saved automatically, with a short notice and an Undo button below the answer.\n\nThe manager lets you search, add, edit and delete memories. A single switch turns memory on or off.\n\nYou can review suggestions before saving them in the pending list. Export and import let you back up your data or move it to another computer."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "![Memory manager][memory-image]"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Install DeepSeek Harness first, then download `dsh-tool-user-memory-0.4.2.tgz` from the [0.4.2 release][release]. Run this command in your download folder and restart DSH afterwards.\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-tool-user-memory-0.4.2.tgz\n```\n\nThe example uses the `web` profile. Replace it with your profile name if needed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "Open Plugins in DSH, find this plugin and click 管理记忆. Saved memories appear in the list, and 新增记忆 adds one manually.\n\nYou do not need to explicitly ask the assistant to remember every personal fact. Clear background, skill familiarity, language and communication preferences can be saved automatically, and the Undo button removes a mistaken addition."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "When enabled, saved memories are included in later conversations. Pending suggestions take effect after you save them, and replacements show the old and new content before confirmation."
    },
    {
      "section": "What gets saved",
      "text": "Only information about you belongs in automatic memory. Project settings, coding constraints, release procedures and temporary requests are skipped, as are unclear statements.\n\nData is stored locally and sent to your configured model provider when used. Turning memory off or deleting it affects future reads, while existing conversations and backups remain."
    },
    {
      "section": "Build from source",
      "text": "Clone the repository, install dependencies and build the plugin. Replace the installation path with your checkout's absolute path.\n\n```sh\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm run build\ndsh plugin --profile web add \"link:/absolute/path/dsh-tool-user-memory\"\n```\n\nWindows paths can use forward slashes, such as `D:/projects/dsh-tool-user-memory`. Restart DSH after rebuilding."
    },
    {
      "section": "Build from source",
      "text": "[npm-badge]: https://img.shields.io/npm/v/dsh-tool-user-memory\n[npm]: https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-tool-user-memory\n[ci-badge]: https://github.com/IAMLieutenant/dsh-tool-user-memory/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg\n[ci]: https://github.com/IAMLieutenant/dsh-tool-user-memory/actions/workflows/ci.yml\n[license-badge]: https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue\n[license]: LICENSE\n[chinese]: README.md\n[release]: https://github.com/IAMLieutenant/dsh-tool-user-memory/releases/tag/v0.4.2\n[changelog]: CHANGELOG.md\n[memory-image]: docs/images/user-memory-list.png"
    }
